cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its generated publication artifacts, please cite
  this archived software release and preserve its evidence-boundary statements.
title: EGMS-Drive Publication Reproducibility
type: software
version: 2.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-26
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Shih-Lin
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0234-8786
    affiliation: National Changhua University of Education
    email: lin040@cc.ncue.edu.tw
abstract: >-
  Code-first reproduction package for the EGMS-Drive manuscript figures,
  tables, compact supplementary material, controlled synthetic mechanism
  analyses, and prospective collision-power analysis. The revised Study 1 is
  a post-hoc exploratory comparison of Baseline B and Structured fusion using
  a method-blind generator, ten paired fitted-model replicates, raw frame and
  episode outputs, checkpoints, exact interval code, and direction-neutral
  validation.
  Studies 2-3 are controlled synthetic surrogates; power outputs are conditional
  planning quantities. The release
  contains no CARLA, public-dataset, real-vehicle, or empirical LLM evidence.
keywords:
  - autonomous driving
  - controlled synthetic mechanism evaluation
  - multisensor fusion
  - paired training replicates
  - raw-output validation
  - temporal scene graph
  - power analysis
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
